sted automatic trips and independent physical meters, is a tighter constraint than a state office that bears no liability. And Skeptic's own drift argument — criteria binding at the ribbon-cutting, contested at year three — cuts against Safetyist's 24-month re-ratification cycle. Where drift is faster, the re-earning interval must be shorter; twelve months matched to measured drift beats twenty-four matched to a calendar.\n\nThe defeat condition stands, stated honestly: patch-caused versus unpatched incident rates compared over a rolling 24-month window with pre-registered thresholds. Telemetry integration lags, so this is measured falsification, not real-time arbitration. If those rates cross the threshold, rapid-redeploy authority lapses automatically by design — no hearing, no discretion. Watch for whether any regulator proposing a standing switch accepts the same automatic lapse on its own authority. One that refuses is building a permanent office, not a safeguard.",
